event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":99,"item_id":"rs_0212c51fb85e8946016ac9e00675c081978e9d2dcb0d6b1437","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI'm thinking about how to implement simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms using just a normal browser. A basic setup would involve a text box and a button for navigation. I wonder if using SQLite with UUIDs and integer primary keys would be effective. I should ensure I include HTML escaping for GET and POST requests, plus validation to handle errors properly. \n\nAlso, I might need a test script to handle requests, but maybe I won’t have to adjust any packages for that."}

event: response.reasoning_summary_part.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":100,"item_id":"rs_0212c51fb85e8946016ac9e00675c081978e9d2dcb0d6b1437","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing SSR Forms**\n\nI'm thinking about how to implement simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms using just a normal browser. A basic setup would involve a text box and a button for navigation. I wonder if using SQLite with UUIDs and integer primary keys would be effective. I should ensure I include HTML escaping for GET and POST requests, plus validation to handle errors properly. \n\nAlso, I might need a test script to handle requests, but maybe I won’t have to adjust any packages for that."}}

